or on  a new sonic game for the sega cd  which would become sonic cd it utilized  the original sonic the hedgehog's code  as a bass  which is probably why sonic cd feels in  my opinion  closer to the original sonic than sonic  2 does it's fairly common knowledge at  this point that sonic 3 was only 50  percent of a complete game  originally yugi knock-in team tried to  create sonic 3 as a  3d game utilizing an svp chip  however this chip wouldn't be ready by  the time they needed it for development  deadlines  thus they were delayed in starting sonic  3 and only completed half of what they  wanted  so they put the rest of the game into  sonic and knuckles and yushinaka came up  with this lock-on technology  which would allow gamers to combine the  two games for one complete experience  what you might not know though is that  other sega games can be combined with  the cartridge for unique add-ons  for sonic 2 you could now play as  knuckles for games older than that you  play a special variation of the sonic 3  knuckles bonus stage  with a layout depending on the cartridge  sonic 1 allows you to play all of these  variations  yuji naka developed this additional  add-on ability completely in secret  with only his development department  knowing about it as they had to test for  bugs  even sega didn't know about this until  the game released  and yushinaka stated all along while i  was creating this trick  i was imagining the looks on children's  faces which made it really fun to do  these additional modes would eventually  be added to gamecube's sonic mega  collection  as the game titled blue  as i mentioned earlier sake of america  and the sonic team along with sega of  japan  didn't always get along and as sonic  became such a major property for the  company  everyone had their own input on what was  best for the series  and one such example comes from the  naming of tales in an internal  competition to create a sidekick for  sonic  yatsushi yamaguchi created the winning  character with tails  however there was a dispute over how to  name him sega japan was convinced miles  per hour  which would sound like miles per hour  was the best way to go  meanwhile sega of america wanted to name  the character tails  even writing a full backstory to the  character to try and convince everyone  that this name was best  finally yamaguchi found the compromise  by using both names  miles per hour would be his real name  and hills his nickname  that last factoid about tailsters is a  great springboard into  the sonic bible  this one's a little better known now  thanks to brian david gilbert's video on  just this topic  at some point allegedly an internal  documented sega of america was spread  a bible for all things related to sonic  the teams could cross-reference while  making future games  shows merchandise toys underwear  fan art oh oh  no what have these eyes seen  anyways this bible includes things like  sonic being born in hartley nebraska  which is different from even the recent  films green hill montana  his dad dying in toxic waste his name  actually being sunny  and his love for chili dog no  whopping beef gloppers what is this  blasphemy  do you like conspiracy theories  no not really i actually think they're  kind of annoying  what if they're true okay  now i'm on board whoa semi  true  it was long rumored that michael jackson  was involved in making the music for  sonic 3.  he was reportedly a huge fan of sega and  there was  of course a michael jackson video game  moonwalker  and thanks to a 2016 huffington post  article written by todd van luling  we now have evidence that's very likely  michael jackson was not  only a fan of sonic but was indeed  involved in helping write sonic 3's  soundtrack apparently the king of pop  decided to pay sti a visit as he was  such a huge fan of sonic 2  and wanted to meet the team behind it  apparently this led to him potentially  helping write the soundtrack to sonic 3.  according to three of the six accredited  songwriters on the game michael jackson  helped write the music  and they would produce high quality  renditions of part of the soundtrack  that would eventually be compressed for  the game  while michael jackson's team was  credited with helping contribute to the  soundtrack  according to them jackson was  disappointed with the compressed  versions of the songs  thus he pulled his name from the credits  according to howard drozen a  california-based composer  jerusalem was under the impression he'd  be working with michael jackson  but eventually told that he wouldn't be  around the time of the major scandal  that michael jackson had allegedly slept  with underage children  according to roger hector an executive  coordinator all the michael jackson's  music was pulled  or replaced meanwhile sega stated it  never worked with jackson on sonic 3 and  refuses to comment on the matter  it's interesting that so many of the  accredited musicians think that  jackson's work was in the game  which leads me to think that this might  actually be true  so there are 12 things you might not  have known about sonic the hedgehog  if you enjoyed this video let us know by  hitting the like button it really does  help  also let me know if you'd like to see  even more sonic the hedgehog facts  as with a 30 year history there is a lot  to cover  what are some of your favorite factoids  about sonic the hedgehog let me know in  the comments below and i'll see you guys  next time  [Music]  [Music]  you

